\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Comprehensive 5-Fold Student Cross-Validation Performance (Test AUC $\uparrow $, Mean $\pm $ Std).} SynapseKT is benchmarked against 19 prior model variants across all 6 standard educational benchmarks. Both mean and standard deviation across the 5 student-disjoint folds are reported to four decimal places (large-scale benchmarks such as \textsc  {NIPS34} and \textsc  {Algebra2005} exhibit small inter-fold standard deviations of $0.0002$--$0.0005$ due to large test sample sizes). Best results are bolded; second-best are underlined. Dashes ($-$) indicate datasets lacking item-level question IDs where Rasch variants reduce to non-Rasch.}}{6}{table.caption.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main_benchmark}{{1}{6}{\textbf {Comprehensive 5-Fold Student Cross-Validation Performance (Test AUC $\uparrow $, Mean $\pm $ Std).} SynapseKT is benchmarked against 19 prior model variants across all 6 standard educational benchmarks. Both mean and standard deviation across the 5 student-disjoint folds are reported to four decimal places (large-scale benchmarks such as \textsc {NIPS34} and \textsc {Algebra2005} exhibit small inter-fold standard deviations of $0.0002$--$0.0005$ due to large test sample sizes). Best results are bolded; second-best are underlined. Dashes ($-$) indicate datasets lacking item-level question IDs where Rasch variants reduce to non-Rasch}{table.caption.10}{}}
